                |The demon in question rests on a bartending counter, heavy tits spilling out of the tight corset she's wearing. When she spots you her tail begins to flick around in anticipation, even while her meaty, flaccid cock no doubt begins to drool out of sight. Not that she's alone, either; 
            ][flags.WAY_P10
                |The shy, smiling form of your bee-bartender sits on a little seat behind the bar.
                |A blushing, nervous-looking bee-girl sits on a little seat behind the bar.
            ][wayfort.hasSatyrs| Two of the satyrs you conscripted are helping Rumie run the bar.]
            |The mess hall looks to be more like a feast hall, with long, polished tables of solid wood, with cushioned benches pushed up to them. Candelabras sit placed at even points to be lit in the dark, and a great stone firepit dominates the central space, filling the entire hall with a comforting warmth[wayfort.hasDaliza
                | and keeping a few cauldrons of strong tea warm for Daliza[wayfort.hasMaids
                    |, the maids, 
                ] and her guard
            ].

            There isn't much need for decoration here, but a few large rugs hang from the wall in order to keep the stone from echoing uncomfortably.

            Last but not least, is the Wayfort's very own bar, a beautiful slice of wooden furniture polished to a mirror sheen by the bumblebee bartender Rumie[wayfort.hasJaelyn
                |, and the ever-grinning, and ever-voluptuous Jael'yn
            ]. Kegs hug the wall beside the doorway to the kitchen and living quarters, and the bar is well stocked with bottles from all over the northern reaches.[wayfort.hasSatyrs| Two of the satyrs you conscripted are helping Rumie run the bar.]

            As you approach, [wayfort.hasMaids
                |a number of maids give way
                |Rumie waves brightly at you
            ]. "Anything [wayfort.hasJaelyn
                |we
                |I
            ] can do for you?"
        ]

        [hed.available
            |Your bird-boy friend, Hed, sits at one of the tables, observing the comers and goers of the tavern. His gaze lingers on [wayfort.hasMaids
                |the maids[wayfort.hasGuards
                    | and certain pretty guards
                ]
                |[wayfort.hasGuards
                    |the guards
                    |certain attractive patrons
                ]
            ] a little longer than modesty would deem appropriate, but no-one seems to be bothered by it. In fact, a couple of people wave or even wink at him — looks like the femboy is rather popular in these parts!
        ]

        [wayfort.furnishingDescription]"

rows.original:
[wayfort.stateABC
    |The fort's servants might have lived here once, crammed into a number of stone bunks cut into the walls. Now it's a home for spiders and rats, running rampant in the absence of an owner. Rotting curtains take the place of doors in the north and south walls.

    One of the bunks has been claimed by Rumie, covered in blankets and pillows of wool and linen respectively, with a couple of mousetraps set out to keep any critters from climbing in.

    [wayfort.hasJaelyn
        |The other bunk has been claimed by Jael'yn; one of the family-sized ones, no less. It's been covered in whatever bedding she must have taken from the Winter City, judging by the incredible quality of it... a rather shocking juxtaposition.
    ]

    [wayfort.hasDrifa
        |With two layers of blankets — a pelt bedspread and a blanket neatly made atop it — and a pillow at one end, Drifa's bunk is as rustic and modest as her. Upon Drifa's bed, you see [drifa.fucked|one of your used shirts|a book] unceremoniously sitting there.[drifa.inHeat| You also smell a distinctly potent scent coming from it.]
    ]

    [wayfort.hasGytha
        |[gytha.isHuntsmaster
            |Gytha's bed is as plain as it gets. The mattress is nothing out of the ordinary, and the only remarkable thing about the blanket that covers it is how diligently it's been stretched to not leave even a single wrinkle. Her pillow is big and otherwise bland looking, but underneath you spot what seems to be a stuffed toy wolf that she's tried to keep hidden[wayfort.hasDaliza
                |, not too different from Daliza's rag-doll. What's with boer'alvar elves and their love for plushies?
            ]
        ]
    ]

    |The living quarters look a lot more, well... lived in. The stone bunks have been carved into to provide a lot more space in exchange for halving the number of accommodations, and a couple of actually decent large beds have been placed in the middle of the room.

    [wayfort.hasDaliza
        |Daliza's bed is a simple thing, with a tough many-folded mattress and a plain duvet... except for what appears to be a soft rag-doll reminiscent of a blue dragon.
    ] 

    [wayfort.hasFarrah
        |Farrah's bed is a decadent silky thing, surprisingly clean and lightly perfumed... looks like she gets up to her fun within the emporium's confines.
    ] 

    [wayfort.hasJaelyn
        |Jaelyn has moved from a stone family bunk to one of these central beds, with extra supports built into it to accommodate her massive muscular form. The bedding is some of the most quality silk and linen you've ever seen, brought over from her previous home in the Winter City.
    ]

    [wayfort.hasDrifa
        |With two layers of blankets — a pelt bedspread and a blanket neatly made atop it — and a pillow at one end, Drifa's bunk is as rustic and modest as her. Upon Drifa's bed, you see [drifa.fucked|one of your used shirts|a book] unceremoniously sitting there.[drifa.inHeat| You also smell a distinctly potent scent coming from it.]
    ]

    [wayfort.hasGytha
        |[gytha.isHuntsmaster
            |Gytha's bed is as plain as it gets. The mattress is nothing out of the ordinary, and the only remarkable thing about the blanket that covers it is how diligently it's been stretched to not leave even a single wrinkle. Her pillow is big and otherwise bland looking, but underneath you spot what seems to be a stuffed toy wolf that she's tried to keep hidden[wayfort.hasDaliza
                |, not too different from Daliza's rag-doll. What's with boer'alvar elves and their love for plushies?
            ]
        ]
    ]

    Rumie the bee's bed looks to be more a nest of blankets than anything, with a simple wooden bucket beside it incase her tits get too full in the night. The whole bed seems to smell like honey and sunshine.

    [wayfort.hasMaids
        |Those maids who choose to stay within your walls during the night have moved comfy leaf-and-cloth made beds into place, giving half of the living quarters a rich, earthy smell that delights the nostrils and smells of a richer, darker honey than Rumie's. [wayfort.hasDaliza
            |Surprisingly enough, it looks a lot like a number of Daliza's soldiers have opted to share bunks with some of the hornets[wayfort.alrauneMaid
                | and alraune effigies
            ]. Cute.
        ]
    ]

    A few beds have been saved for your companions; warm affairs of simple wool, cotton, and linen... You, on the other hand, have the only separate room in the living quarters, with a heavy wooden door that leads to a soft queen-sized bed of thick fluffy blankets and sheets, some of which have been embroidered with little black and white crowns. The fireplace is functional, though it could use some moderate repairs. At the very least it has an ever-necessary quantity of thick logs, which crackle merrily in order to keep the northern chill at bay.
    |The living quarters look almost royal now. Every stone bunk has been expanded to accommodate multiple willing guards and servants, and the large beds in the middle of the room have been given some far-improved wooden frames, guaranteed to last a lifetime.

    [wayfort.hasDaliza
        |Daliza's bed is a simple thing, with a tough many-folded mattress and a plain duvet... except for what appears to be a soft rag-doll reminiscent of a blue dragon.
    ]

    [wayfort.hasFarrah
        |Farrah's bed is a decadent silky thing, surprisingly clean and lightly perfumed... looks like she gets up to her fun within the emporium's confines.
    ]

    [wayfort.hasJaelyn
        |Jaelyn has moved from a stone family bunk to one of these central beds, with extra supports built into it to accommodate her massive muscular form. The bedding is some of the most quality silk and linen you've ever seen, brought over from her previous home in the Winter City.
    ]

    [wayfort.hasVatia
        |[vatia.hasKids
            |Vatia <i>would</i> be by the firepit if not for the way she's being pulled in all directions by your three children. It looks as though she's got her hands full.
            |Vatia is over by the firepit.
        ]
    ]

    [wayfort.hasDrifa
        |With two layers of blankets — a pelt bedspread and a blanket neatly made atop it — and a pillow at one end, Drifa's bunk is as rustic and modest as her. Upon Drifa's bed, you see [drifa.fucked|one of your used shirts|a book] unceremoniously sitting there.[drifa.inHeat| You also smell a distinctly potent scent coming from it.]
